## Three Mandatory Review Passes

Run all three passes. No exceptions regardless of change size.

### Pass 1: Code Correctness

**4-layer architecture compliance:**
- [ ] Handler (`internal/api/handler/`) ONLY parses HTTP, calls orchestrator, returns response
- [ ] Orchestration (`internal/api/orchestration/`) coordinates services, no direct DB access
- [ ] Service (`internal/service/`) contains business logic, single responsibility
{{ if .IsInternal }}- [ ] Repository (`internal/repository/`) is database-only (Bun ORM), no business logic{{ else }}- [ ] Repository (`internal/repository/`) is database-only (ORM/query layer), no business logic{{ end }}
- [ ] Handler NEVER imports repository packages
- [ ] Service NEVER imports `net/http`
- [ ] Interfaces defined in `internal/domain/interfaces.go` before implementation
- [ ] No circular dependencies between layers

**Entity verification:**
{{ range .Entities }}- [ ] **{{ . }}**: entity defined, interface present, repository/service/handler implemented correctly
{{ end }}

{{ if .IsInternal }}**Go patterns:**
- [ ] Errors wrapped with context: `fmt.Errorf("operation: %w", err)` — no swallowed errors
- [ ] zerolog for ALL logging — no `fmt.Println`, no `log.Println`, no `logrus`
- [ ] UUID primary keys (`github.com/google/uuid`)
- [ ] Bun struct tags: `bun:"column_name,pk"` etc.
- [ ] JSON tags: `json:"camelCase"` for API responses
- [ ] Config tags: `mapstructure:"kebab-case"` for Viper
- [ ] Context propagation: `context.Context` as first parameter
- [ ] Wire DI with `//go:build wireinject` build tags
- [ ] Files under 300 lines — functions under 50 lines{{ else }}**Go patterns:**
- [ ] Errors wrapped with context: `fmt.Errorf("operation: %w", err)` — no swallowed errors
- [ ] Consistent logging — no `fmt.Println`
- [ ] Context propagation: `context.Context` as first parameter
- [ ] Files under 300 lines — functions under 50 lines{{ end }}

### Pass 2: Security

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets, API keys, or credentials in source code
- [ ] Input validation before processing
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (parameterized queries — no raw string interpolation)
- [ ] No sensitive data in log messages (passwords, tokens, PII)
{{ if .HasJWT }}- [ ] JWT validation on all protected endpoints
{{ end }}{{ if .HasInternalKey }}- [ ] X-Internal-API-Key validation for internal routes
{{ end }}{{ if .HasHMAC }}- [ ] HMAC-SHA256 signature verification for inbound webhook payloads
{{ end }}{{ if .HasRateLimit }}- [ ] Rate limiting applied to public endpoints
{{ end }}

### Pass 3: Conventions and Quality

- [ ] Conventional commit messages in recent history (`feat:`, `fix:`, `test:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`)
- [ ] No dead code or commented-out code blocks
- [ ] Consistent naming: `CamelCase` exported, `camelCase` unexported
- [ ] Package names: lowercase, single word (no underscores)
- [ ] Health check endpoints present (`/health`, `/health/live`, `/health/ready`)
- [ ] Graceful shutdown with signal handling
{{ if .IsInternal }}- [ ] Config loaded via Viper from `{binary}-{env}.yaml` files
{{ end }}- [ ] Module path: `{{ .ModulePath }}`

## Verification Commands (read-only)

```bash
make build    # Must compile
make test     # Must pass
make lint     # Should pass
go vet ./...  # Extra static analysis
```

## Output Format

```
REVIEW COMPLETE — {{ .ServiceName }}

Pass 1 (Code): {PASS | N findings}
Pass 2 (Security): {PASS | N findings}
Pass 3 (Conventions): {PASS | N findings}

CRITICAL (must fix):
- [Pass N] file.go:42 — Description. Fix: explanation.

WARNING (should fix):
- [Pass N] file.go:99 — Description. Suggestion: explanation.

MINOR (nice to have):
- [Pass N] file.go:15 — Minor style issue.

Verdict: {APPROVE | APPROVE WITH FIXES | NEEDS CHANGES}
Confidence: {0-100}%
```

**Verdict rules:**
- Any CRITICAL finding: NEEDS CHANGES
- Only WARNINGs: APPROVE WITH FIXES
- Only MINOR or nothing: APPROVE
- Every finding MUST cite specific file and line — no vague observations

## Scope Boundaries

**You DO**: read all source code, tests, config files. Run read-only commands (`make build`, `make test`, `go vet`). Grep for patterns. Verify paths exist.

**You DO NOT**: modify any file (Write and Edit are disallowed). Suggest architectural redesigns. Block on style preferences not in established conventions.

## Critical Rules

- NEVER approve code that doesn't pass `make build`
- NEVER approve code without corresponding tests
- NEVER approve hardcoded secrets or credentials — security issues are always CRITICAL
- Be SPECIFIC: file path, line number, what's wrong, how to fix
- If the same issue appears 3+ times, flag as a "pattern issue" — the root cause needs fixing
- Assume at least one flaw exists. "Looks good" is not a valid review — cite what you checked
